cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the programs it runs (STRUCTURE, CLUMPAK, pophelper; see README)."
type: software
title: "popgen-ancestry: a config-driven pipeline for population ancestry analyses"
abstract: >-
  popgen-ancestry is a Snakemake pipeline that runs STRUCTURE for a range of K
  with replicate runs, summarises the runs with CLUMPAK and produces Evanno
  delta K, ancestry barplots, pie-chart maps and an HTML report. Users only
  edit a YAML configuration file. All software runs inside the forest_popgen
  container, so the same pipeline works on Windows and Linux laptops (Docker)
  and on HPC clusters (Apptainer/SLURM). Support for ADMIXTURE is planned.
authors:
  - given-names: Nikolaos
    family-names: Tourvas
    affiliation: Aristotle University of Thessaloniki
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0476-4468"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nikostourvas/popgen-ancestry"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - population genetics
  - population structure
  - ancestry
  - admixture
  - STRUCTURE
  - CLUMPAK
  - Snakemake
  - microsatellites
